# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CIO Executive Dashboard — environment template
#
# There are TWO environment files, and they are not the same thing:
#
#   .env.local  — local development (`npm run dev`). Copy this file to it.
#   .env        — the Docker stack on the box. GENERATED, not hand-written:
#                 `node ops/generate-secrets.mjs --hostname <tailnet host>`
#
# NEVER commit either. `.gitignore` already excludes them. The repository is
# public: every secret lives only on your box.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Self-hosted Supabase — runs on your Windows/WSL2 box, reachable over
# Tailscale. Use the tailnet hostname of that box, e.g.
#   https://dashboard.your-tailnet.ts.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only. Bypasses Row Level Security — keep OUT of the browser and OUT
# of git. Only read in server-side code; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Field encryption (Phase 2)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Encrypts mail bodies and OAuth tokens at the field level, so a leaked backup
# or a `pg_dump` does not hand over the mailbox. Without it, the Full caching
# policy refuses to run and account credentials cannot be stored at all.
#
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log('v1:' + require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# Rotation is additive — add `v2:...`, point ACTIVE_KEY at it, and keep the old
# key until every row has been rewritten. Each stored value carries its key id.
#
# BACK THIS UP OFF THE BOX. Losing it makes every stored body and token
# unreadable.
DASHBOARD_ENCRYPTION_KEYS=
DASHBOARD_ENCRYPTION_ACTIVE_KEY=v1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mail and calendar providers (Phase 2)
# See docs/oauth-setup.md. Redirect URIs use the tailnet hostname.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google — Gmail and Calendar.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Microsoft 365 — optional. The adapter is built and tested; leaving these
# empty simply means the provider is listed but not offered. Adding them turns
# it on with no code change.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Only for a single-tenant Azure registration.
# MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=

# Proton, through Proton Bridge running on this box. The username and the
# Bridge-generated password are entered in the app and stored encrypted.
# PROTON_BRIDGE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PROTON_BRIDGE_IMAP_PORT=1143
# PROTON_BRIDGE_SMTP_PORT=1025

# Domains treated as internal when deciding whether a meeting is external.
# Comma-separated. Feeds Phase 5's ranking.
# DASHBOARD_INTERNAL_DOMAINS=theonefor.ai

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Observability
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Labels error reports. "development" locally, "production" on the box.
DASHBOARD_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Leave EMPTY unless you have decided you want error reports to leave the
# box. Empty means errors are logged locally and go nowhere else. Reports are
# scrubbed either way (src/lib/observability/scrub.ts), but the trade-off is
# yours to make — see docs/threat-model.md § 4.7.
#
# Enabling it also needs the package installed on the box, which this
# repository deliberately does not depend on:
#   npm install @sentry/nextjs
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Testing only — never set these on the box.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `memory` swaps the Supabase repository for an in-process one and bypasses
# auth so Playwright can run without a database. It is ignored entirely when
# NODE_ENV=production, so a production build cannot be put into this mode.
# DASHBOARD_DATA_MODE=memory

# Postgres connection string for the RLS integration tests. When unset those
# tests skip. CI provides a throwaway container; locally you can point it at a
# scratch database — never at the one holding your real data.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
